IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bkv-law`
IMPORT `bkv-worker-law`

-- Seat layer: a worker who has a disease and asks whether it is a listed occupational disease: entry No. 1322 of Anlage 1 BKV, Parkinson syndrome from long-term, frequent and self-applied pesticides.
-- It asks that person's questions, takes plain facts as inputs, builds the law layer's record internally and calls the law layer's rules. It restates no rule. Target compiler: main.
-- The article by Ringe and Folkerts argues that the Seventh Amending Regulation is void for want of citing the power for its change to § 9(5) BKV. It does not argue that the new entry falls; the second question below asks what follows if the whole Regulation falls (NOTES.md, forks F2 and F14).
-- The answer is yes, no, or nothing for a disease the encoding does not cover. A 'no' on the void reading does not decide whether the disease can still be recognised like an occupational disease under § 9(2) SGB VII.

§ `Is my disease a listed occupational disease?`

@export Is my disease a listed occupational disease, entry No. 1322 of Anlage 1 of the Occupational Diseases Regulation (Parkinson syndrome from long-term, frequent and self-applied pesticides), reading the Seventh Amending Regulation as in force since 1 August 2026? Answers yes or no, and nothing for a disease this encoding does not cover.
GIVEN
    `my disease`             IS A `Disease of the worker` @desc Which disease you have: Parkinson syndrome, or another disease. This encoding covers only the Parkinson syndrome of entry No. 1322; for another disease it answers nothing.
    `caused by pesticides`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Parkinson syndrome was caused by pesticides you used at work. The accident insurer finds the cause in your case; answer as you expect it to decide.
    `used for many years`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you applied pesticides over many years (the entry says 'langjährig'). The entry gives no figure; answer as you expect the insurer to decide.
    `used often`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you applied pesticides often (the entry says 'häufig'). The entry gives no figure; answer as you expect the insurer to decide.
    `applied by myself`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you applied the pesticides yourself (the entry says 'selbst angewendete'), and not only worked where others applied them.
    `in insured work`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the pesticide use was part of work covered by the statutory accident insurance (an activity within § 2, 3 or 6 of Book VII of the Social Code). This is a legal characterisation; answer as you expect the insurer to decide.
    `the date`               IS A DATE @desc The day for which you ask whether the disease is listed, such as the day you make your request to your accident insurer, written like 2026-08-01.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is my disease a listed occupational disease with the Seventh Amending Regulation in force` MEANS
    `the disease is a listed occupational disease under the reading` `the Seventh Amending Regulation stands` case
    WHERE
        case MEANS `Case of a worker with a disease` WITH
            `the disease` IS `my disease`
            `the disease was caused by pesticides` IS `caused by pesticides`
            `the pesticides were applied over many years` IS `used for many years`
            `the pesticides were applied often` IS `used often`
            `the pesticides were applied by the worker` IS `applied by myself`
            `the pesticide use was part of work covered by statutory accident insurance` IS `in insured work`
            `the date of the request` IS `the date`

-- The next group only arises if you ask what follows if the whole Seventh Amending Regulation is void, which is a reading of the article's argument that it does not itself make.
-- A form can ask "Do you want to know what follows if the whole Regulation is void?" before showing it.
§ `What if the whole Seventh Amending Regulation is void?`

@export Is my disease a listed occupational disease, entry No. 1322 of Anlage 1 of the Occupational Diseases Regulation, if the whole Seventh Amending Regulation (Federal Law Gazette 2026 I Nr. 210) is void, as it would be if a defect in citing the power for its change to § 9(5) voided the Regulation entire? Answers yes or no, and nothing for a disease this encoding does not cover. A no does not decide whether the disease can still be recognised like an occupational disease under § 9(2) of Book VII of the Social Code, a route the Federal Government's memorandum says gives the same benefits.
GIVEN
    `my disease`             IS A `Disease of the worker` @desc Which disease you have: Parkinson syndrome, or another disease. This encoding covers only the Parkinson syndrome of entry No. 1322; for another disease it answers nothing.
    `caused by pesticides`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Parkinson syndrome was caused by pesticides you used at work. The accident insurer finds the cause in your case; answer as you expect it to decide.
    `used for many years`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you applied pesticides over many years (the entry says 'langjährig'). The entry gives no figure; answer as you expect the insurer to decide.
    `used often`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you applied pesticides often (the entry says 'häufig'). The entry gives no figure; answer as you expect the insurer to decide.
    `applied by myself`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you applied the pesticides yourself (the entry says 'selbst angewendete'), and not only worked where others applied them.
    `in insured work`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the pesticide use was part of work covered by the statutory accident insurance (an activity within § 2, 3 or 6 of Book VII of the Social Code). This is a legal characterisation; answer as you expect the insurer to decide.
    `the date`               IS A DATE @desc The day for which you ask whether the disease is listed, such as the day you make your request to your accident insurer, written like 2026-08-01.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is my disease a listed occupational disease if the Seventh Amending Regulation is void as a whole` MEANS
    `the disease is a listed occupational disease under the reading` `the Seventh Amending Regulation is void as a whole` case
    WHERE
        case MEANS `Case of a worker with a disease` WITH
            `the disease` IS `my disease`
            `the disease was caused by pesticides` IS `caused by pesticides`
            `the pesticides were applied over many years` IS `used for many years`
            `the pesticides were applied often` IS `used often`
            `the pesticides were applied by the worker` IS `applied by myself`
            `the pesticide use was part of work covered by statutory accident insurance` IS `in insured work`
            `the date of the request` IS `the date`

§ `Did the 2026 amending regulation cite the power for the new occupational disease?`

@export Does the preamble of the Seventh Regulation amending the Occupational Diseases Regulation (Federal Law Gazette 2026 I Nr. 210) cite § 9(1) sentences 1 and 2 of Book VII of the Social Code, the power to designate diseases as occupational diseases? Answers yes or no, from the gazette text of the preamble.
`does the 2026 preamble cite the power for the new occupational disease` MEANS
    `the preamble of the Seventh Amending Regulation cites the power to list a disease`
